{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/291263-dead-dominions-ala-ravenloft","id":291263,"title":"Dead Dominions ala Ravenloft","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-24T06:41:50-07:00","id":291263,"title":"Dead Dominions ala Ravenloft","content":"Thought this could be a fun little idea to try out, but what if the Dead Dominions of the Underworld were each akin to a Dark Realm found within D&amp;D's Ravenloft? With the darklords being <i>deathlords</i> being tormented by whatever commands the kerberos of said-realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:09:57-07:00","id":291484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/291263-dead-dominions-ala-ravenloft#post291263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought this could be a fun little idea to try out, but what if the Dead Dominions of the Underworld were each akin to a Dark Realm found within D&amp;D's Ravenloft? With the darklords being <i>deathlords</i> being tormented by whatever commands the kerberos of said-realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they were separate things, keberoi and death/darklords.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem with this is that Ravenloft domains are predicated on the mundane population of unfortunates stuck in with the darklords. Underworld Dominions are inhabited by, well, the dead. They passed being mundane a <i>long </i>time ago. That, and it's implied deathlords in general, while not precisely kind, are honorable and fair (see Mictlantechli Polydegmon, whose torment of his supplicants are primarily meant to make damned sure the supplicant is willing to go through hell to get a specific soul back, and it is implied he's a true deathlord as well as a keberos).<br /> <br /> So, honestly, the themes kind of conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T15:20:39-07:00","id":291597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/291263-dead-dominions-ala-ravenloft?p=291484#post291484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if they were separate things, keberoi and death/darklords.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem with this is that Ravenloft domains are predicated on the mundane population of unfortunates stuck in with the darklords. Underworld Dominions are inhabited by, well, the dead. They passed being mundane a <i>long </i>time ago. That, and it's implied deathlords in general, while not precisely kind, are honorable and fair (see Mictlantechli Polydegmon, whose torment of his supplicants are primarily meant to make damned sure the supplicant is willing to go through hell to get a specific soul back, and it is implied he's a true deathlord as well as a keberos).<br /> <br /> So, honestly, the themes kind of conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Shit, I thought I had a match made in heaven right there. :&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:47:48-07:00","id":291622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/291263-dead-dominions-ala-ravenloft?p=291597#post291597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Shit, I thought I had a match made in heaven right there. :&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That isn't to say you can't, but the idea is probably best confined to one specific Dead Dominion themed around punishment and how denial of what we really want is the real torture. The idea is that eventually, ghosts realize this and let go, going down. Darklords could be those who just can't let themselves let go, both because they were obsessive even in life, and because they can't admit they ruined their own existence in the process of getting what they wanted. The keberos could be the most powerful, the idea of one simply being the strongest ghost has canon merit (the Victor of the Junkyard, for instance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:03:11-07:00","id":292237,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T05:55:43-07:00","id":292909,"title":"","content":"Hrm... A nice middle ground: make it a full on &quot;layer&quot; or &quot;level&quot; of the underworld. All Dead Dominions on this level fit a Ravenloft-esque theme, but serve the same purpose Leliel said earlier. This should give you the scope and the feel you want, while preserving the themes of the underworld. It should probably be a high-ish level, but not the first one. Probably like, three, or something.<br /> <br /> Oh, one thing to understand if you do this is the difference that perspective is going to make. Per the default mode of play, Ravenloft pits you as a weak-ish mortal in the face of horrors that are simply beyond the players. They are as much a slave to the realms as the lords are. In Geist, Sin Eaters can choose to simply not be there. They are also, by default, much closer in power to what you'll present as Dark Lords. Instead of being slaves to the realm, Sin Eaters would be in a position to directly examine the darklords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 10-26-2014, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T16:46:11-07:00","id":296293,"title":"","content":"I think the Ravenloft domains would make great True Fae dominions if you remove the meta aspect of Ravenloft with the higher powers behind the scenes. If you want to keep it to the Underworld then I think you can take some elements from Ravenloft, but a direct port does have some problems of theme between Geist and Ravenloft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}